1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,900
Ask a model about your shop's refund policy, and it will guess. Retrieval augmented generation gives it the right page first, like an open-book exam.

2
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:20,725
Find the few chunks that match the question, put only those into the prompt, and ask it to answer only from them.

3
00:00:22,430 --> 00:00:31,005
A simple way: count how many of the question's important words appear in each chunk, ignoring words like the and is.

4
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:39,475
Better systems use embeddings, which match meaning, not just words. You will meet them later in this course.

5
00:00:40,180 --> 00:00:47,305
Send only the top few chunks. More is not better: irrelevant text confuses the model.

6
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:54,400
Number the sources, and ask the model to cite them, so people can check.

7
00:00:55,100 --> 00:01:04,975
And always add the rule: if the sources do not contain the answer, say I don't know. An honest gap is better than a confident guess.

